 "brief": "Gaza's education sector is launching an exceptional academic year under unprecedented conditions, Shehab Wire reported. Mohamed Abu Jaser, deputy chairman of Gaza's teachers' union, emphasized that the coming term cannot be measured by conventional readiness standards, as the territory faces an abnormal educational landscape.\n\nThe school year begins after years of forced interruption to learning in the strip, according to Abu Jaser's statement. Teachers are preparing to resume instruction despite the extraordinary circumstances confronting the education system.",
